1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,180
He sank a ship, then rescued hundreds of survivors and was bombed for it.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:11,010
In September 1942 U-156 was off the coast of West Africa.

3
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:17,930
On the evening of 12 September, commander Werner Hartenstein torpedoed the British troopship Laconia.

4
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:20,770
About 2,700 people were on board:

5
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:28,660
British soldiers, civilians including women and children, Polish guards and about 1,800 Italian prisoners of war.

6
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:34,710
When U-156 surfaced, the crew heard cries for help in Italian from the water.

7
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:40,260
Hartenstein realised he had also hit soldiers of his own ally, and began a rescue.

8
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:45,820
He took survivors on board until the deck was full of people, and took lifeboats in tow.

9
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:53,110
Then he radioed openly in English that he would not attack any ship helping the survivors, as long as he was not attacked himself.

10
00:00:53,190 --> 00:00:57,770
Dönitz sent more U-boats, and an Italian submarine came to help as well.

11
00:00:57,790 --> 00:01:07,400
On 16 September U-156, with a large Red Cross flag on the bridge, headed for the French ships that were to take over the survivors.

12
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:11,480
Then an American B-24 bomber appeared.

13
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,240
The crew reported the sighting to Ascension, and from there came the order to attack.

14
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:20,760
A bomb struck among the lifeboats, and dozens of survivors died.

15
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:24,810
Hartenstein had to send the people on his deck into the water and dived.

16
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:29,110
The next day French warships picked up most of the survivors.

17
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:36,000
Even so, more than 1,600 people died in total, most of them Italian prisoners.

18
00:01:36,050 --> 00:01:41,280
Dönitz responded with the Laconia Order: no U-boat was to rescue survivors any more.

19
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:44,670
After the war this order was held against him at Nuremberg.

20
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:50,260
But the court did not find it proven that he had thereby ordered the killing of survivors.

21
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:52,370
Hartenstein did not live to see it.

22
00:01:52,390 --> 00:02:02,100
In March 1943 an American aircraft sank U-156 east of Barbados, and the entire crew was lost.
